{title: The Wonderful Cross}
{artist: Gateway Worship}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Verse 1}
[D]When I survey the w[G]ondrous c[D]ross
[D]On which the pr[G]ince of gl[D]ory d[A]ied,
[D]My richest gain I co[G]unt but l[D]oss,
[D]And pour c[A]ontempt on [C2]all my pri[D]de.

{comment: Verse 2}
See from his head, His hands, His feet,
Sorrow and love flow mingled down.
Did e'er such love and sorrow meet,
Or thorns compose so rich a crown.

{comment: Chorus}
[D]O the [G]wonderful cross[D],
O the [G]wonderful cross[D]
Bids me c[G]ome and die
and f[D]ind that I may t[A]ruly live.
O the [G]wonderful c[D]ross,
O the [G]wonderful c[D]ross
All who g[G]ather here
By [D]grace draw near and [A]bless your name.

{comment: Verse 3}
Were the whole relm of nature mine,
That were an of-f'ring far to small.
Love so amazing so divine,
Demands my soul, my life, my all.

{comment: Chorus}
